SM(169,{"n":"James 1.16 - 2.13","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/James 1.16 - 2.13.mp3","d":2444.9,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Council of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[22.32,"Verse 16, do not be deceived, my beloved brethren."],[25.84,"Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and comes down from the Father of Lights, with whom there is no variation or shadow of turning."],[37.6,"You may recognize that from part of the prayer behind the Anvon at the end of the end of the liturgy."],[44.72,"But so notice, see, he's saying the other side."],[47.12,"Don't be deceived."],[47.92,"On the other side, all every good thing that comes to us in our life comes from God."],[54.0,"Right. Every good thing."],[58.16,"And with him, there's no variation or shadow of turning."],[63.68,"He's not going to change his mind about us one day."],[67.2,"Right? He's not sending us good things one day and bad things the next day, because he's in a bad mood."],[75.2,"He's not going to turn away from us."],[76.8,"We may turn away from him, but he's not going to turn away from us."],[80.56,"That's what he's saying."],[83.6,"Verse 18, of his own will he brought us forth by the word of truth that we might be a kind of first fruits of his creatures."],[94.0,"So uh word of truth isn't capitalized there, but should be."],[100.56,"It's talking about Christ."],[103.52,"The word of God."],[105.6,"Which was firmly established for Jewish people in the Old Testament tradition as being a way to refer to the second person of the Trinity."],[116.08,"Right. This isn't just a thing in St."],[117.6,"John's Gospel. St."],[118.64,"James would have been aware of this too."],[119.92,"He brought us forth."],[120.44,"Right? God created everything through his word through his logos."],[123.88,"Right? And that's what he's talking about."],[126.44,"He created us by his logos."],[129.08,"Which we see in Genesis."],[130.44,"This is the common interpretation of Genesis."],[132.44,"So it should be capital W word of truth."],[135.0,"That we might be a kind of first fruits of his creatures."],[138.52,"Right? Of all the things he created, humanity is the first fruits."],[143.32,"Which puts us above angels, referring back to Hebrews."],[147.64,"Right? If we're the first fruits."],[157.0,"Right? Or something different than what St."],[158.84,"Paul was teaching, or is it this the same stuff we've been reading?"],[163.24,"It's the same same kind of thing."],[165.4,"Right? And so what's he saying here?"],[167.4,"Right? Again, the evil stuff in our life doesn't come from God."],[171.8,"It comes from us."],[173.72,"Right? All the good in our life comes from God."],[178.44,"Right? All the good stuff comes from God, who is not going to change his attitude toward us."],[183.72,"And who created us in the first place?"],[187.16,"Right? And created us out of love."],[189.96,"Because he loves us and desires us."],[194.6,"Right? That's what that's what St."],[196.84,"James is saying here."],[197.64,"And that's the contrast."],[199.24,"Right. So if you take temptation to be like, hey, do you want this piece of cake?"],[204.6,"Right? You're not supposed to have."],[207.0,"Homer Simpson's forbidden donut."],[209.48,"Like, if you take it that way, then the contrast with all good things come from God doesn't make a ton of sense."],[217.48,"But if he's talking about the evil in the world, right, that we face as a trial, compared to everything good comes from God, then it does make a lot of sense."],[224.36,"Right. And again, sorry, Calvinists, that means everything doesn't come from God."],[237.44,"Verse 19, so then, my beloved brethren, this so then is serving the same kind of function as St."],[244.96,"Paul's therefore. It's therefore in this trust."],[247.52,"Okay. Yeah. So this is basically therefore."],[252.96,"Based on what we just said, my beloved brethren."],[256.56,"Let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, and slow to wrath."],[262.88,"For the wrath of man does not produce the righteousness of God, the justice of God."],[267.84,"Right? So he's talking about that justice."],[270.32,"Things being put in order."],[273.36,"So you getting angry about things is not going to bring about God's justice."],[280.32,"Right? Even if you're angry at injustice."],[283.12,"Even if you're angry at injustice, that anger is not going to produce justice."],[289.52,"And this is sort of evergreen, but also very important now."],[295.6,"Right? Violence, rioting, revolutions, does not produce justice if we're talking about God's justice."],[303.6,"Ever. That includes all violent revolutions."],[308.32,"Including the favorite one from your own country."],[311.2,"Right? That doesn't produce justice."],[313.76,"That's not how God's justice is brought about, is by our wrath and anger and violence."],[320.32,"It will never produce it."],[323.84,"Right? And therefore, since that doesn't work."],[328.64,"That doesn't work."],[329.6,"Right. We need to be swift to hear."],[332.36,"We need to spend more time listening to God."],[337.32,"More time listening to God."],[338.76,"And less time talking."],[341.16,"And even less time being angry."],[346.36,"Right. So the anger here, specifically that anger directed towards changing things."],[352.28,"Right? Towards doing our will."],[354.2,"Right? Accomplishing our will."],[356.68,"Right? That's why it builds off of speaking."],[360.6,"Rather than listening to God and what God says about things, we want to give our own opinion and then try to enforce that through anger and violence on the world around us."],[371.72,"Right. And that is not what's going to produce the justice of God."],[376.68,"That's not what's going to set things right."],[382.36,"Verse 21, therefore lay aside all filthiness and overflow of wickedness, and receive with meekness the implanted word which is able to save your souls."],[394.6,"Right. So all that bad stuff, too, obviously, that you're out there doing."],[400.84,"That filthiness, all the uncleanness."],[405.72,"Like the overflow of wickedness."],[409.8,"The imagery there is that we've got this sort of wickedness inside of us."],[414.6,"And it overflows out into actions."],[418.36,"Out into the world."],[420.36,"So we need to get rid of that."],[422.52,"We need to get rid of what's flowing out of us."],[425.56,"And instead focus on what God has placed within us."],[431.16,"Right. So our talking, our anger coming out from us versus hearing, listening to God."],[441.76,"Right? And now the word that's placed within us, the seed that's planted within us by God that can grow into our salvation versus us."],[452.64,"Vomiting out what's in us into the world."],[456.4,"That's the contrast he's making."],[460.24,"Verse 22, but be doers of the word and not hearers only, deceiving yourselves."],[467.36,"Right. So again, see St."],[469.92,"James keeps he keeps clarifying his points."],[472.96,"Right? So he says, I'm not saying by that that you don't do anything."],[477.76,"Right? When I say focus on receiving from God, not on putting what's in you out into the world, I don't mean don't do anything."],[486.88,"Right. Right. So once you've heard the word, once you've received the word, once you've received Christ, right, you then need to put Christ Christ into action."],[498.88,"Right. But do you see how that's different than putting what's within me into action out into the world?"],[508.16,"Right. So what St."],[512.08,"James is saying is I have to acknowledge that I, in and of myself."],[516.64,"I, Father Stephen D."],[518.0,"Young, as a human person, have nothing worthwhile to offer out into the world that comes from me."],[527.6,"Right. If you read one of my books, and in there you find a truly original idea from me, reject it because it's false."],[538.32,"Right? Anything that's in there that where I'm passing on what I've received, that's what you should pay attention to."],[547.64,"So that's what St."],[549.64,"James is saying."],[551.16,"Right? We need to receive Christ."],[554.44,"Right? But then we need to offer Christ out into the world."],[559.56,"We need to act and live our lives like Christ, in faithfulness to Christ in the world."],[565.56,"Not in faithfulness to ourselves, not be true to myself."],[571.24,"My own identity, what I have to offer, my unique individuality, my vision."],[578.68,"My theorizing, my genius."],[582.12,"Whatever it is."],[583.32,"Right? St. James is saying all that stuff's garbage."],[586.84,"Right? You focus on truly receiving Christ and then on giving Christ out to the world."],[594.36,"Right. But don't just be one of those people who receives Christ and then does nothing."],[600.36,"Right? Well, does that remind you of anything in St."],[602.68,"Matthew's gospel? Remember the parable of the talents?"],[608.6,"Right? Where they receive Tells of Silver, the one guy goes and buries it."],[613.4,"Right? And then loses even what he had."],[617.88,"Verse 23 for if anyone is a hearer of the word and not a doer, he is like a man observing his natural face in a mirror."],[626.2,"For he observes himself, goes away, and immediately forgets what kind of man he was."],[632.12,"So he's making an analogy."],[634.12,"Right? So this is like, you know, if you just hear it and you don't do anything."],[639.72,"And you don't put it out of the world."],[642.12,"That's like being a person who goes and looks in a mirror and you see what you look like, and then you walk away and forget what you look like."],[648.24,"This may exist in an age where there were very few mirrors, and you very seldom saw yourself in one, and so it was easy to forget."],[656.08,"Yeah. My my more uh my more contemporary example that I give, because this is something I do all the time, is this is like somebody who looks at their watch or their phone to see what time it is and then puts it back in their pocket or puts it back down and still has no idea what time it is, and you have to look again."],[678.16,"Right? And then you feel kind of dumb."],[681.68,"And that's exactly what St."],[683.2,"James is saying."],[684.24,"That's kind of dumb."],[686.64,"Right? To hear it and not do anything with it."],[692.72,"Verse 25, but he who looks into the perfect law of liberty and continues in it, and is not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this one will be blessed in what he does."],[707.84,"So it's the person who you look into the law of liberty, but oh see, he likes the law, and St."],[717.12,"Paul hated the law."],[719.12,"Thank you for playing."],[720.32,"We already talked about that."],[721.68,"Right? The one who looks into it."],[725.2,"And remembers what's in it, and does it."],[730.64,"That's the one who is blessed."],[735.12,"Right? That's the one who is doing what uh God has called them to do."],[740.16,"Like St. Paul says at the beginning of Romer, Romans, it's not the hearers of the law, but the doers who are justified."],[748.24,"Sounds like pretty much the same thing."],[749.84,"St. Right that St."],[752.04,"Paul and St."],[753.72,"James are saying."],[755.0,"And of course, both of them are drawing on."],[758.76,"This was the problem in the Old Testament."],[762.6,"Right? The Old Testament is not a triumphant story of Israel."],[766.6,"Everything that can go wrong goes wrong."],[769.32,"Right. And, you know, there was a whole generation of people who stood at the bottom of Mount Sinai and received the law, received the Torah."],[780.2,"Receive the commandments."],[781.4,"And they even swore that they'd keep all of them."],[783.56,"And then they kept none of them."],[786.36,"Right? They all heard it."],[788.52,"They didn't do it."],[789.56,"They all died in the desert."],[792.68,"Right? This is where they're getting this."],[795.08,"We're all capable."],[796.68,"You can come to liturgy every Sunday and on feast days and hear all the hymns and hear all the scripture readings."],[806.04,"And then just sort of go back about living your life however you want to, it's not going to do you any good."],[813.24,"Having been there and heard it."],[816.52,"Right? It's like looking at your phone and still not knowing what time it is."],[828.84,"Verse 26. If anyone among you thinks he is religious and does not bridle his tongue, but deceives his own heart, this one's religion is useless."],[840.68,"Pure and undefiled religion before God and the Father is this."],[845.96,"To visit orphans and widows in their trouble, and to keep oneself unspotted from the world."],[854.0,"So putting the word religious in here is right kind of skews it."],[862.48,"Yeah. It's really more like piety."],[866.64,"And we have a very different."],[871.52,"Right. So when we think of somebody being really religious, we think, well, they they go to church a lot."],[880.08,"They they do certain actions."],[883.2,"They spend a lot of time praying."],[885.76,"They do. Um piety in the ancient world was conceived of as a moral virtue."],[894.8,"Right? Like by Aristotle, say, in the Nicomachean Ethics, just as an example."],[901.2,"And piety is that there is a certain sort of reverence that is due to the gods for a pagan."],[913.28,"Or to God, right, in this case."],[915.84,"There's a certain reverence that's due."],[918.24,"There are certain commandments that he's placed upon you, demands that he's placed upon you, especially if we're talking about a Jewish context."],[925.76,"And if you fulfill those, right, then you're a pious person, and if you don't, then you're an impious person."],[934.0,"Right? Was sort of the idea."],[935.92,"And if you're an impious person, that was a moral failing."],[940.0,"Right? That made you not a very good person."],[943.92,"Low quality person."],[947.92,"So this that's more the idea here of piety or religion that St."],[953.28,"James is appealing to here."],[955.36,"Right? So he's saying if you're someone who thinks, like, oh, I've met my obligations to God."],[959.92,"I've got that squared away."],[962.76,"Right. Right. But you are a person who does not bridle your tongue."],[974.44,"Right? You don't control your mouth and what you say."],[979.4,"Right. Then all that box checking you've done on your religious duties."],[986.68,"Is worthless. Right?"],[989.8,"Is worthless. Right."],[992.04,"And this is that idea that we were talking about before, like that you see in the prophets."],[996.2,"Stop it with the sacrifices."],[999.0,"I don't care about you checking the boxes."],[1001.0,"Your heart is far from me."],[1002.92,"This is the same kind of idea."],[1004.44,"You may be checking all those boxes."],[1006.92,"But if there's all kinds of, like Christ said, it's from the overflow of the heart that the mouth speaks."],[1013.88,"And there's all kinds of evil coming out of your mouth, then it doesn't matter that you checked all those boxes."],[1022.44,"Right. And so it says, pure and undefiled religion before God and the Father is this."],[1033.4,"Right. So if you want to be a pious person, if you want to fulfill that, right, then this is what you need to do."],[1044.52,"Right? Not show up at certain times and celebrate certain feasts and those kind of things."],[1049.32,"But visit orphans and widows in their trouble."],[1052.92,"That visit isn't like stop by and say hi."],[1055.64,"Hi, orphans. Or what else?"],[1059.4,"This is visit is in come and assist."],[1062.2,"Right? Widows and orphans."],[1063.64,"Widows and orphans all through the old testament, they're sort of the paradigmatic helpless people in that society."],[1070.8,"Because they had no legal rights."],[1072.72,"They were totally dependent on other people."],[1074.8,"If other people were kind to them and loved them and showed charity to them, they could have a good life."],[1080.72,"If people turned away from them, they would die of starvation."],[1085.28,"Right. Or they could abuse the people could abuse them at will and they had no legal recourse."],[1090.48,"Right? Even worse."],[1092.64,"So this is emblematic of just the helpless in general."],[1096.8,"By arguing for the extreme case."],[1099.6,"Right. Um just orphans and widows in their trouble and keep oneself unspotted from the world."],[1108.4,"Right? Don't become involved in the filth of the world."],[1113.52,"Right. Um again, here's another parallel to St."],[1120.4,"Matthew's gospel. When Christ in St."],[1123.44,"Matthew's Gospel talks about the last judgment that we read on the Sunday of the last judgment, the parable of the sheep and the goats."],[1131.2,"Why do the sheep go to heaven and the goats go to hell?"],[1135.44,"Right? Why visited the followers and widows?"],[1139.12,"Yes. Yes. They gave us it to the weak, the poor, the sick, those in prison."],[1149.12,"Those helpless people."],[1151.04,"Right? That's the criteria for who's pious and who's impious."],[1156.8,"Who's right with God?"],[1157.6,"Who isn't? St."],[1158.8,"James is saying the same thing."],[1162.16,"Right? That Christ said."],[1164.0,"This is emblematic."],[1166.32,"Right? This is emblematic."],[1168.08,"Because, right, love your neighbors, your neighbor as yourself."],[1170.0,"Your fellow human is the image of God."],[1174.12,"Right? And in the ancient world, and even today, what you do to an image of someone, you are symbolically doing to them."],[1183.96,"Right? If I held up a took a picture of one of your family members and spit on it or threw it on the ground and stomped on it in front of you, you would not be like, ah, it's just a picture."],[1195.48,"Right? You would be insulted."],[1197.56,"Because you would know what I meant by that."],[1200.76,"Right? And so if every human being we encounter is in the image of God, then whatever we do to them, whatever we say to them, however we treat them, we're doing to God."],[1213.16,"Right. So if you wouldn't do it with an icon here in the church, you shouldn't do it to your fellow human being."],[1221.56,"And if you would do it to an icon here in the church, you should do it to your fellow human being in terms of caring for them and protecting them."],[1230.44,"Um, so that's the idea."],[1232.12,"That's why that is an act of piety."],[1236.52,"Right? As Christ also says, the one who gives a cup of cold water, right, to one of these little ones."],[1244.6,"Right? It doesn't have to be a grand gesture."],[1246.92,"You don't have to buy somebody a house."],[1249.16,"Can't even buy myself a house."],[1251.24,"But but whatever we do, right, we are doing that to God and for God."],[1258.92,"And so everything becomes an act of piety or of impiety."],[1264.12,"Right, on the flip side."],[1270.84,"Okay. So chapter two."],[1278.16,"My brethren, do not hold the faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Lord of glory, with partiality."],[1287.36,"Let's pause there."],[1291.68,"With hypocrisy? Yeah."],[1293.6,"Yeah. By pausing first for another, we'll get to that."],[1296.4,"But I'm pausing first for another reason."],[1298.48,"Okay. So one of our things about those Jewish Christians, those imaginary Jewish Christians back in the in the past, who are this separate group, is that they didn't think Jesus was God, supposedly."],[1312.32,"Right? They just thought he was like a human Messiah."],[1315.68,"Right? He was the king."],[1317.04,"And it's St."],[1317.84,"Paul with all this Greek stuff that starts bringing in all this Trinity stuff and this polytheism stuff."],[1325.44,"Uh. Except, right here, Saint James calls his brother, who he watched grow up, the Lord of glory."],[1342.72,"Oops. Right. And we talked about we've talked before about how of is a punt when you're translating Greek."],[1351.84,"Right? It means it's a genitive."],[1353.84,"Right? What this really means is the glorious Lord."],[1358.08,"This is Old Testament language for Yahweh, the God of Israel."],[1362.16,"That's St. James is applying to his kid stepbrother."],[1368.16,"So very clearly, St."],[1370.16,"James, at least, who is supposed to be the leader of these Jewish Christians, thinks that Jesus is divine."],[1378.48,"Pretty clearly. And that the faith of is also, again, punting."],[1380.28,"Right. Right? Because the reason I say punting is you can interpret that a lot of ways."],[1388.84,"The faith of our Lord Jesus Christ."],[1390.2,"So is that saying Christ's faith?"],[1393.96,"Like his faith?"],[1395.16,"His faithfulness. So it's a it's a punt."],[1404.68,"But the idea is that do not."],[1409.8,"Do not attempt to be faithful to our Lord Jesus Christ with partiality."],[1413.88,"Right? Meaning those two things are incompatible."],[1417.16,"Right? Those two things are you cannot follow Christ and then be partial."],[1423.48,"Or as that has be a be a hypocrite."],[1426.36,"And we'll see what that means here."],[1429.24,"Right. You you and this is continue off of what we just said."],[1435.4,"Right? So it's continuing this idea about I'm pious."],[1438.6,"I'm one of the faithful."],[1440.92,"Right? I'm one of the."],[1442.84,"So it's if you think you're pious, but you're doing this, eh-right?"],[1448.12,"And now this is in parallel."],[1450.44,"So if you think you're being faithful to Christ, but you're showing this partiality or you're showing this hypocrisy, eh."],[1459.4,"Right. So what does he mean by this partiality or this hypocrisy?"],[1463.16,"Verse 2. For if there should come into your assembly, and the word assembly, there's the word church."],[1469.32,"Actually, it's synagogue, but someone comes into your gathering, your religious gathering."],[1476.52,"A man with gold rings in fine apparel, and there should also come in a poor man in filthy clothes, and you pay attention to the one wearing the fine clothes, and say to him, You sit here in a good place, and say to the poor man, you stand there, or sit here at my footstool."],[1495.68,"Have you not shown partiality among yourselves and become judges with evil thoughts?"],[1502.64,"Right. So he's saying."],[1510.32,"Because he's saying, in your assembly."],[1512.72,"Your different assemblies, your different communities."],[1516.4,"You have these communities, and someone comes in who's very clearly rich."],[1520.48,"You're like, oh, it's so nice to see you today."],[1524.64,"Thank you for visiting."],[1526.16,"Thank you for joining our worship."],[1527.76,"Here, come sit here."],[1528.72,"Here's a spot for you."],[1530.64,"Right? You can meet the priest afterward."],[1533.28,"You know, hey, let's get your number."],[1535.6,"We want to see you again."],[1537.68,"And then someone comes in who's sheveled looking, who's filthy."],[1542.8,"Looks homeless in our modern language."],[1544.56,"And you go, oh, yeah, no, no, no, no, go sit over there."],[1547.92,"Right? Don't be asking anybody for money."],[1552.56,"Right? Then what does St."],[1554.24,"James say? When you do that, you're being a judge with evil thoughts."],[1559.12,"Now that doesn't sound that bad to us."],[1561.92,"I mean, obviously, it's not a good thing to be a judge with evil thoughts."],[1565.36,"But this is appealing to something in the Torah."],[1568.16,"Right? This is the foremost command to the leaders in Israel."],[1574.72,"To the elders of Israel, right, who are gonna serve as judges."],[1580.56,"They were supposed to establish justice, make sure things happened well."],[1584.4,"God says, He is the God who loves the orphan and the widow."],[1589.36,"It shows no partiality and will not take bribes."],[1594.04,"Right? And so what makes a wicked judge in the Torah, who is threatened with the worst kinds of condemnation, is someone who favors the wealthy over the poor, who favors the powerful over the powerless."],[1611.24,"Who takes bribes."],[1613.72,"Right. So St."],[1615.64,"James is saying here."],[1617.56,"He's playing off this idea."],[1618.76,"He very clearly has in mind, again, this idea we saw in St."],[1622.04,"Paul, and that we're gonna see again in St."],[1623.72,"Peter's epistles that come up next."],[1626.52,"Um, that not only is the Church Israel, right, but that every member of the Christian community, because we have the Holy Spirit, is on the level of those judges of Israel."],[1643.16,"Right? We are all in that leadership position."],[1646.36,"Right? And therefore, all of those commands to that leadership also apply to us."],[1656.28,"Right. And therefore, we have to be impartial and not accept bribes, and not favor, right, those who we think have something to offer us over those who we think don't."],[1672.12,"Right? Because that person with the money who we want to court to get them to donate money to the church is not more valuable to God than the homeless person who has nothing to offer and who needs our help."],[1686.76,"In fact, in some cases, the opposite, depending on the state of the wealthy person's heart."],[1691.56,"Remember the rich man in Lazarus."],[1693.76,"Right? Right? God desires the salvation of both of those people."],[1701.84,"But what may help that rich man's salvation, remember what we just read in chapter one?"],[1706.16,"Maybe his humiliation."],[1709.44,"He may have to humble himself if he's going to find salvation."],[1714.24,"And us fawning over him and telling him how wonderful he is, so that he'll give us money is not going to help him find salvation."],[1725.04,"Right? And us disregarding this person who's equally precious to God, but who has nothing to offer to us and may smell bad and be filthy."],[1733.84,"It's not helping his salvation either."],[1738.64,"And so St."],[1739.44,"James is pointing to what the church is all about, it's about helping us all find salvation."],[1745.2,"Everybody who walks in the door, including us."],[1749.28,"And us being unjust judges is not helping our salvation either."],[1754.16,"So what he's putting forward here, which is a completely commonplace thing in churches to this very day, is for St."],[1762.48,"James a worst case scenario."],[1766.16,"This is the worst thing that could be going on in your churches."],[1770.08,"We don't think of it that way."],[1772.4,"Because we're so used to it."],[1774.48,"Right? We think the worst thing that could be happening would be, I don't know, probably sexual immorality in our modern churches."],[1783.36,"Somebody cheating on their spouse or, you know, somebody stealing from the church, stealing money from the church."],[1790.48,"Those are the things that we think would be the worst things that could be happening in the church, probably."],[1794.48,"For St. James, this is the worst thing that could be happening in your church."],[1798.72,"Right? Because somebody could be stealing money from the church, and the people of the church could still find salvation."],[1807.24,"Right? And not just could be, everybody in the church is sinning all the time."],[1812.04,"I know, I hear the confessions."],[1814.28,"Right. Everybody in the church is sinning all the time."],[1819.08,"But those even those people find salvation in the church."],[1823.32,"Right? But when this is going on."],[1827.72,"This isn't helping anybody's salvation."],[1831.32,"And that's what the church is about."],[1833.64,"Not about the grass that dries up and withers and blows away."],[1837.32,"Having the shiny new dome and the big new building that's going to crumble."],[1843.08,"Right? That's not what the church is about."],[1845.96,"This is what the church is about."],[1848.12,"Helping people find salvation."],[1855.24,"Verse 5, listen, my beloved brethren."],[1857.8,"Has God not chosen the poor of this world to be rich in faith and heirs of the kingdom, which he promised to those who love him?"],[1867.88,"Obviously, this is a rhetorical question."],[1870.84,"Right? That it's yes."],[1872.52,"Right? Because who did Christ come and peach preach to?"],[1877.8,"Was right, yeah."],[1878.76,"Was he was he born the son of the Roman Emperor and uh went to the Senate to proclaim the good news?"],[1887.96,"No. He was born dirt poor and preached to other Galilean peasants."],[1893.72,"Right? And that's who he chose to be as apostles."],[1897.72,"Right? A bunch of fishermen."],[1902.04,"And so he says this these are the people who God chose."],[1904.84,"Right. So who are the people who you choose to honor?"],[1912.96,"Verse 6, but you have dishonored the poor man."],[1916.8,"Do not the rich oppress you and drag you into the courts?"],[1919.84,"Do they not blaspheme that noble name by which you are called?"],[1924.32,"Right? So he's saying, and this is just as true today."],[1927.76,"Let's look at the wealthy and powerful of the world."],[1930.72,"Are they the people who most love Christ?"],[1935.2,"Are they supporting you and your church?"],[1939.36,"Right? Are these the these are the people you should aspire to be like?"],[1944.16,"Are these the people whose favor whose favor you should be courting?"],[1949.04,"Right? Again, rhetorical question."],[1952.08,"Obvious answer, no."],[1955.52,"Verse 8, if you really fulfill the royal law according to the scripture, you shall love your neighbor as yourself, you do well."],[1966.56,"Who said that was one of the most important commandments?"],[1969.52,"One of the two."],[1971.52,"Christ. St. Matthew's gospel."],[1976.48,"You do well."],[1977.36,"But if you show partiality, you commit sin."],[1980.48,"And are convicted by the law as transgressors."],[1985.04,"Right? So if you don't love your neighbor, your neighbor here being everybody."],[1995.12,"As yourself, then you've sinned."],[1998.96,"And you're transgressors."],[2000.48,"Verse 10 for whoever shall keep the whole law and yet stumble in one point, he is guilty of all."],[2007.36,"For he who said do not commit adultery also said do not murder."],[2011.48,"Now, if you do not commit adultery, but you do murder, you have become a transgressor of the law."],[2017.48,"Right? So what's he saying?"],[2019.24,"Remember, we're talking about people who think they're pious."],[2021.96,"People who think they're faithful."],[2023.48,"That's how he started this."],[2024.68,"You think you're faithful to Christ, but you show this partiality."],[2029.16,"Right? And he's saying, hey, if you don't if you fail to love your neighbor as yourself, then you've broken the law."],[2036.36,"And it doesn't matter if you keep most of the rest of it."],[2039.48,"Right? A guy who commits murder can't be like, yeah, but I never cheated on my wife."],[2044.2,"So I'm not all bad."],[2045.8,"It's like, no, you're still a murderer."],[2048.44,"Right? You're still a murderer."],[2050.28,"You're still a transgressor."],[2051.4,"You're still a sinner."],[2053.0,"Right? So he's saying it doesn't matter if you keep all this other stuff."],[2056.36,"It doesn't matter if you're faithful to your wife, and you're you're attending the services and saying the prayers, and you don't lie, and you don't, but if you mistreat your brother because he's poor."],[2072.84,"Right? And mistreat in the opposite way the rich man who comes into the church who needs salvation."],[2079.16,"If you're not loving your neighbor as yourself, then it doesn't matter if you keep all the other stuff."],[2092.68,"Verse 12, so speak and so do as those who will be judged by the law of liberty."],[2099.08,"For judgment is without mercy to the one who has shown no mercy."],[2103.56,"Mercy triumphs over judgment."],[2108.68,"Why does he keep saying the law of liberty?"],[2110.6,"Why doesn't he just say the law?"],[2112.76,"Right? The law of freedom."],[2114.88,"Right? The law which sets you free."],[2117.12,"Well, remember, we gotta go back to St."],[2120.24,"Paul and Romans again."],[2122.0,"Remember, he talked about within the within the heading of law of gnomos."],[2127.44,"Of Torah. He talked about the letter and the spirit."],[2131.84,"Those are subsections of that."],[2134.08,"Because what does the Holy Spirit do?"],[2135.68,"The Holy Spirit writes the law in our hearts."],[2138.96,"Right. So for Saint James, he uses this to connote that, the law of freedom."],[2146.96,"Meaning the law is fulfilled in Christ."],[2150.72,"Right? Which is still the Torah."],[2152.48,"It's not a different law."],[2154.4,"Right? It's not different commandments."],[2156.48,"Right? Love your neighbor as yourself comes from Leviticus."],[2161.04,"So, same law, but as fulfilled in Christ."],[2165.92,"As we're now set free by the Spirit to fulfill it, not in the old way."],[2172.0,"Right. So, this is the same kind of qualifier that St."],[2176.72,"Paul uses. When St."],[2178.96,"Paul talks about the law, that nuance, as we saw, gets lost by people."],[2182.8,"Oh, he just didn't like the law."],[2183.92,"It's like, no, no, no, no, no, no."],[2185.76,"Right? But he made a distinction between the law as fulfilled in Christ that we follow and the way that his fellow Pharisees who had accepted Christ wanted to follow and impose the law."],[2198.88,"Right? Particular parts of it, especially."],[2202.24,"But right, that now we're seeing fulfilled in Christ."],[2205.28,"That's the same thing Saint James is doing here."],[2209.52,"And so we need to speak and to do."],[2213.52,"Our works and our words."],[2215.84,"As those who will be judged by the law of liberty."],[2219.8,"That that last judgment is going to come."],[2222.52,"Right. And we've received these commandments."],[2225.4,"We've received the word."],[2227.16,"We've received Christ."],[2228.76,"We're going to be judged by what we did with it."],[2233.24,"Right? Which is what Christ says over and over and over again."],[2236.36,"Right? That we're judged according to our works."],[2240.28,"And so we need to keep that in mind when we're acting."],[2244.92,"And he says, for judgment is without mercy to the one who has shown no mercy."],[2249.96,"Right? Which is the reverse of what Christ says in one of the Beatitudes."],[2253.88,"Blessed are the merciful, for they will be shown mercy."],[2258.2,"So if you show no mercy to the poor man."],[2262.84,"This poor destitute person needs your help."],[2264.92,"Why would you expect God to show mercy to you?"],[2269.16,"Right? Remember also the parable of uh the evil steward, the one who has forgiven."],[2277.24,"The huge debt, and then went out and attacked the guy who owed him a couple of bucks."],[2283.24,"And then ended up being thrown in prison."],[2284.92,"He had his forgiveness revoked."],[2287.4,"Because he would not forgive."],[2289.8,"Right? That's a constant theme in St."],[2291.88,"Matthew's gospel again, in Christ's preaching."],[2295.64,"That forgive us our debts as we forgive our debtors."],[2299.56,"That those go in parallel."],[2301.0,"It's the same thing he's saying here."],[2302.52,"So if you want us, you're gonna be judged one day by God."],[2308.44,"Saying, right now, right, we're in that judge position, remember?"],[2311.8,"That's the analogy he used."],[2314.52,"Right? You're serving as a judge."],[2316.36,"God has entrusted you with this role in your community."],[2320.68,"In your church, this authority God has given you, right, for the purpose of helping each other find salvation."],[2324.84,"That's been entrusted to you."],[2329.6,"And if when you're tasked with this, with being a judge, you show partiality and you don't show any mercy, and you show favoritism."],[2342.16,"Why would you then, when you stand before God, expect him to show mercy to you?"],[2348.96,"Right? And not show favoritism to you."],[2362.4,"Oh, now we get into the controversial part."],[2366.24,"Oh. Oh. Cliffhanger."],[2372.64,"We're gonna pick up here next time."],[2376.88,"Yeah. Yeah, because we've got on a fair amount now."],[2380.8,"And uh we're about to open the proverbial can of worms."],[2386.08,"We're about to read the section that uh got a certain old Luther in Germany very upset at the Epistle of St."],[2399.36,"James. Um yeah, we'll we'll stop here."],[2402.72,"We'll stop here at the end of verse 13, and we'll pick up in uh James 2, 14, and get into all that and whether this is really disagreeing with St."],[2413.12,"Paul, uh next time."],[2418.96,"So thank you, everybody."],[2422.48,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the whole council of God."],[2429.6,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecouncil at ancientfaith.com."],[2435.24,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":22.32,"lv":2,"h":"1:16-18 - Every good gift from above","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:16</b> \"Do not be deceived, my beloved brethren\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Every good and perfect gift</b> from above, from the <b>Father of Lights</b></li><li class=\"d1\">part of the prayer behind the ambon, end of liturgy</li><li class=\"d0\">Notice \"the other side\": <b>every good thing</b> in our life comes from God</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>No variation or shadow of turning</b></li><li class=\"d1\">won't \"change his mind about us one day\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not sending good one day, bad the next \"because he's in a bad mood\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>we</b> may turn from him; <b>he won't</b> turn from us</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:18</b> \"of his own will he brought us forth by the word of truth\"</li></ul>"},{"t":94.0,"lv":3,"h":"The Word of truth - first fruits","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Word of truth\" should be <b>capital W</b> - it is <b>Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Word of God</b> = established in Jewish OT tradition as way to refer to the <b>second person of the Trinity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just a St. John thing; <b>James</b> would have known it</li><li class=\"d0\">God created everything through his word, his <i>logos</i></li><li class=\"d1\">\"he created us by his <i>logos</i>\" - seen in <b>Genesis</b>, common interpretation</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>First fruits</b> of his creatures</li><li class=\"d1\">of all he created, <b>humanity is the first fruits</b></li><li class=\"d1\">puts us <b>above angels</b> - back to <b>Hebrews</b></li></ul>"},{"t":165.4,"lv":3,"h":"Evil comes from us, not God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Same kind of thing as Paul - same stuff we've been reading</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Evil</b> in our life doesn't come from God - comes from <b>us</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>All the good</b> comes from God</li><li class=\"d1\">who won't change attitude toward us</li><li class=\"d1\">who <b>created us</b> in the first place - <b>out of love</b>, \"he loves us and desires us\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Reading of \"temptation\" as <b>trial</b> makes the contrast work</li><li class=\"d1\">if temptation = \"do you want this piece of cake?\" - <b>Homer Simpson's forbidden donut</b></li><li class=\"d1\">then \"all good things come from God\" makes no sense</li><li class=\"d1\">evil we face as a trial vs. everything good from God = makes sense</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Sorry, <b>Calvinists</b>\" - everything doesn't come from God</li></ul>"},{"t":237.44,"lv":2,"h":"1:19-20 - Swift to hear, slow to wrath","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:19</b> \"so then\" = same function as Paul's <b>\"therefore\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">based on what we just said</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:20</b> wrath of man doesn't produce the <b>righteousness / justice of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">justice = things <b>put in order</b></li><li class=\"d1\">your anger won't bring God's justice - <b>even if angry at injustice</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Evergreen, but very important now\"</li></ul>"},{"t":295.6,"lv":3,"h":"Violence never produces justice","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Violence, rioting, revolutions</b> - never produce God's justice</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Ever.\" Includes <b>all violent revolutions</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"including the favorite one from your own country\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God's justice not brought about by <b>our wrath, anger, violence</b> - \"will never produce it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Since that doesn't work → be <b>swift to hear</b></li><li class=\"d1\">more time <b>listening to God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">less time talking; even less time angry</li><li class=\"d0\">Anger here = anger aimed at <b>changing things, doing our will</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why it builds off <b>speaking</b></li><li class=\"d1\">instead of listening to God, we give <b>our own opinion</b> and enforce it with anger and violence</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not what's going to set things right\"</li></ul>"},{"t":382.36,"lv":2,"h":"1:21 - Lay aside filth, receive the implanted word","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:21</b> lay aside <b>filthiness and overflow of wickedness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">receive with <b>meekness</b> the <b>implanted word</b> - able to save your souls</li><li class=\"d0\">Filthiness = all the <b>uncleanness</b> \"you're out there doing\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Overflow</b> imagery</li><li class=\"d1\">wickedness inside us <b>overflows</b> into actions, out into the world</li><li class=\"d1\">get rid of what's flowing out of us</li><li class=\"d1\">focus on what <b>God has placed within us</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Contrast</li><li class=\"d1\">our <b>talking, anger</b> coming out vs. <b>hearing, listening to God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the word = <b>seed planted by God</b> → grows into our <b>salvation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">vs. us \"vomiting out what's in us into the world\"</li></ul>"},{"t":460.24,"lv":2,"h":"1:22 - Doers of the word","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:22</b> \"be <b>doers</b> of the word and not hearers only, deceiving yourselves\"</li><li class=\"d0\">James \"keeps clarifying his points\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not saying don't do anything</li><li class=\"d0\">Once you've <b>received Christ</b> → <b>put Christ into action</b></li><li class=\"d1\">different from putting <b>what's within me</b> into action</li><li class=\"d0\">Receive from God, then <b>offer Christ</b> out into the world</li><li class=\"d1\">act and live \"in faithfulness to Christ in the world\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> faithfulness to myself: \"be true to myself\", my identity, unique individuality, vision, \"my theorizing, my genius\"</li><li class=\"d1\">James: \"all that stuff's <b>garbage</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":508.16,"lv":3,"h":"Nothing original from me","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">I, <b>Fr Stephen De Young</b>, in myself have <b>nothing worthwhile</b> to offer the world from me</li><li class=\"d0\">\"If you read one of my books and find a <b>truly original idea</b> from me, <b>reject it - it's false</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">pay attention to where I'm <b>passing on what I've received</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Don't be one who receives Christ and then <b>does nothing</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>parable of the talents</b>, Matthew</li><li class=\"d1\">receives talents of silver, one <b>buries</b> it</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>loses even what he had</b></li></ul>"},{"t":617.88,"lv":2,"h":"1:23-24 - The man and the mirror","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:23</b> hearer not doer = man observing his <b>natural face in a mirror</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sees himself, walks away, <b>immediately forgets</b> what he looked like</li><li class=\"d0\">Hear it and put nothing out into the world = same</li><li class=\"d0\">Ancient age: <b>very few mirrors</b>, seldom saw yourself → easy to forget</li><li class=\"d0\">His modern example - \"something I do all the time\"</li><li class=\"d1\">look at your <b>watch or phone</b> for the time, put it away, <b>still no idea what time it is</b></li><li class=\"d1\">have to look again - \"then you feel kind of dumb\"</li><li class=\"d0\">James: \"that's <b>kind of dumb</b>\" - to hear and do nothing with it</li></ul>"},{"t":692.72,"lv":2,"h":"1:25 - The perfect law of liberty","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:25</b> looks into the <b>perfect law of liberty</b>, <b>continues</b> in it, not a forgetful hearer but a <b>doer</b> → <b>blessed</b> in what he does</li><li class=\"d0\">James likes the law; \"Paul hated the law... thank you for playing\" - already covered</li><li class=\"d0\">Blessed one = looks in, <b>remembers what's in it, does it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doing what God has called them to do</li><li class=\"d0\">Parallel: Paul, start of <b>Romans</b> - not hearers of the law but <b>doers justified</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"pretty much the same thing\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Both draw on the <b>OT problem</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a \"triumphant story of Israel\" - \"everything that can go wrong goes wrong\"</li><li class=\"d1\">generation at <b>foot of Sinai</b> received Torah, <b>swore to keep all</b> - then <b>kept none</b></li><li class=\"d1\">heard, didn't do → <b>all died in the desert</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same for us: liturgy every Sunday, feasts, hymns, readings → then live as you want = <b>no good</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"like looking at your phone and still not knowing what time it is\"</li></ul>"},{"t":828.84,"lv":2,"h":"1:26-27 - Bridle the tongue; pure religion","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:26</b> thinks he is religious, doesn't <b>bridle his tongue</b>, deceives his heart → religion <b>useless</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:27</b> pure and undefiled religion = <b>visit orphans and widows in trouble</b>, keep <b>unspotted from the world</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Religious\" skews it - really more like <b>piety</b></li></ul>"},{"t":862.48,"lv":3,"h":"Piety as a moral virtue","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">We hear \"religious\" = goes to church a lot, does certain actions, much prayer</li><li class=\"d0\">Ancient world: <b>piety = moral virtue</b></li><li class=\"d1\">e.g. <b>Aristotle</b>, <i>Nicomachean Ethics</i></li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>reverence due</b> to the gods (pagan) or to God</li><li class=\"d1\">certain <b>commandments, demands</b> - esp. Jewish context</li><li class=\"d1\">fulfill them = <b>pious</b>; don't = <b>impious</b></li><li class=\"d1\">impious = <b>moral failing</b> - \"low quality person\"</li><li class=\"d0\">This is the sense James appeals to</li></ul>"},{"t":955.36,"lv":3,"h":"Box-checking with an unbridled tongue","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Person thinks \"I've met my obligations to God, got that squared away\"</li><li class=\"d0\">But doesn't <b>control his mouth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">all the <b>box checking</b> on religious duties = <b>worthless</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Like the <b>prophets</b>: \"stop it with the sacrifices, I don't care about you checking boxes\" - <b>\"your heart is far from me\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Christ</b>: from the <b>overflow of the heart</b> the mouth speaks</li><li class=\"d1\">evil coming out of your mouth → doesn't matter you checked the boxes</li></ul>"},{"t":1022.44,"lv":3,"h":"Visit orphans and widows","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Pure and undefiled religion\" = how to be pious</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> showing up at certain times, celebrating certain feasts</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Visit</b> isn't \"stop by and say hi\" - means <b>come and assist</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Widows and orphans</b> throughout OT = <b>paradigmatic helpless</b> of that society</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no legal rights</b>, totally dependent</li><li class=\"d1\">kindness and charity → good life; turned away → <b>starvation</b>, or <b>abused at will</b> with no recourse</li><li class=\"d1\">emblematic of <b>the helpless in general</b> - \"arguing for the extreme case\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Unspotted from the world</b> = don't get involved in the <b>filth of the world</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1113.52,"lv":3,"h":"Sheep and goats; the image of God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Parallel: <b>Matthew</b>, last judgment - <b>parable of sheep and goats</b> (Sunday of the Last Judgment)</li><li class=\"d1\">sheep to heaven, goats to hell: they gave to the <b>weak, poor, sick, prisoners</b> - the helpless</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>criteria for who's pious and impious</b>, right with God</li><li class=\"d0\">Emblematic: <b>love your neighbor as yourself</b>; fellow human = <b>image of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ancient world and today: what you do to an image, you do <b>symbolically to the person</b></li><li class=\"d1\">spit on / stomp a <b>picture of your family member</b> - \"you'd be insulted\"</li><li class=\"d1\">whatever we do to any human → we do to <b>God</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Icon test</b>: wouldn't do it to an icon in church → don't to a human; would → do it (caring, protecting)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cup of cold water</b> to one of these little ones</li><li class=\"d1\">no grand gesture - \"can't even buy myself a house\"</li><li class=\"d1\">everything becomes an act of <b>piety or impiety</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1270.84,"lv":2,"h":"2:1 - Faith of the Lord of glory, without partiality","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 2:1</b> \"do not hold the faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Lord of glory, with <b>partiality</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Pausing first on <b>\"Lord of glory\"</b> (partiality later)</li><li class=\"d0\">Imaginary <b>Jewish Christians</b> as separate group</li><li class=\"d1\">supposedly didn't think Jesus was God - just <b>human Messiah, king</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul with \"Greek stuff\" brings in <b>Trinity, polytheism</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Here James calls his brother</b> - whom he watched grow up - the <b>Lord of glory</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1342.72,"lv":3,"h":"\"Of\" is a punt","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Of</b> is a punt\" when translating Greek - it's a <b>genitive</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Lord <b>of glory</b>\" = really <b>the glorious Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">OT language for <b>Yahweh, God of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">James applies it to his \"kid stepbrother\"</li><li class=\"d1\">→ James, supposed leader of the Jewish Christians, thinks Jesus is <b>divine</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Faith <b>of</b> our Lord\" also a punt</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ's own faith? his <b>faithfulness</b>? many ways to read</li><li class=\"d0\">Idea: don't try to be faithful to Christ <b>with partiality</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>incompatible</b> - can't follow Christ and be partial / a <b>hypocrite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">continues the \"I'm pious, one of the faithful\" thought, now in parallel</li></ul>"},{"t":1463.16,"lv":2,"h":"2:2-4 - The rich man and the poor man","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:2-4</b> man with <b>gold rings, fine apparel</b>; poor man in <b>filthy clothes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"you sit here in a good place\" / \"you stand there, or sit at my footstool\"</li><li class=\"d1\">→ <b>shown partiality, judges with evil thoughts</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Assembly\" = word for church; actually <b>synagogue</b>, religious gathering</li><li class=\"d0\">Modern version</li><li class=\"d1\">rich visitor: \"so nice to see you... come sit here... meet the priest... let's get your number\"</li><li class=\"d1\">disheveled, \"looks homeless\": \"go sit over there... don't be asking anybody for money\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Judge with evil thoughts\" doesn't sound that bad to us</li></ul>"},{"t":1565.36,"lv":3,"h":"Judges and the Torah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Appeals to the <b>Torah</b>: foremost command to <b>elders of Israel</b> serving as judges</li><li class=\"d1\">establish justice; God loves <b>orphan and widow</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no partiality, no bribes</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Wicked judge</b> = favors <b>wealthy over poor</b>, powerful over powerless, takes bribes</li><li class=\"d1\">threatened with the <b>worst condemnation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same idea as <b>Paul</b>; coming again in <b>Peter's epistles</b></li><li class=\"d1\">church is Israel <b>and</b> every member, with the <b>Holy Spirit</b>, is on the level of those <b>judges</b></li><li class=\"d1\">all in that <b>leadership position</b> → all those commands apply to us</li><li class=\"d0\">Impartial; no bribes; no favoring those who might <b>have something to offer us</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Rich donor not more valuable to God than the <b>homeless person</b> who needs help</li><li class=\"d1\">sometimes the opposite - depends on the rich person's <b>heart</b>; <b>rich man and Lazarus</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1693.76,"lv":3,"h":"Both need salvation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">God desires the <b>salvation of both</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Rich man: maybe his <b>humiliation</b> (ch. 1) - must <b>humble himself</b></li><li class=\"d1\">fawning, \"so he'll give us money\" won't help his salvation</li><li class=\"d0\">Disregarding the poor man - equally precious, \"may smell bad and be filthy\" - doesn't help his salvation either</li><li class=\"d0\">Church = <b>helping us all find salvation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">everybody who walks in, <b>including us</b></li><li class=\"d1\">us being <b>unjust judges</b> doesn't help ours</li></ul>"},{"t":1754.16,"lv":3,"h":"The worst thing in your church","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Commonplace in churches to this day - for James <b>worst-case scenario</b></li><li class=\"d0\">We'd say worst = <b>sexual immorality</b>, cheating on a spouse, <b>stealing from the church</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why James differs</li><li class=\"d1\">church could have a thief and people still find salvation</li><li class=\"d1\">\"everybody in the church is sinning all the time - <b>I hear the confessions</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">even they find salvation <b>in</b> the church</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>partiality</b> helps nobody's salvation</li><li class=\"d0\">Church is <b>not</b> about the grass that withers</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"the shiny new <b>dome</b>, the big new building that's going to crumble\"</li><li class=\"d1\">it's about <b>helping people find salvation</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1855.24,"lv":2,"h":"2:5-7 - God chose the poor","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:5</b> \"Has God not chosen the <b>poor of this world</b> to be <b>rich in faith</b> and heirs of the kingdom?\" - rhetorical</li><li class=\"d0\">Who did Christ preach to?</li><li class=\"d1\">not born son of the <b>Roman Emperor</b> proclaiming good news to the Senate</li><li class=\"d1\">born <b>dirt poor</b>, preached to <b>Galilean peasants</b></li><li class=\"d1\">chose <b>fishermen</b> as apostles</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Who are the people <b>you</b> choose to honor?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:6-7</b> you dishonored the poor; do not the <b>rich oppress you, drag you into courts, blaspheme the noble name</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"just as true today\"</li><li class=\"d1\">wealthy and powerful - most love Christ? supporting your church? people to aspire to, court?</li><li class=\"d1\">rhetorical - obvious answer <b>no</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1955.52,"lv":2,"h":"2:8-11 - The royal law","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:8</b> fulfill the <b>royal law</b>: \"love your neighbor as yourself\" → you do well</li><li class=\"d1\">one of the <b>two</b> great commandments - <b>Christ</b>, Matthew</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:9</b> show partiality → <b>commit sin</b>, convicted as <b>transgressors</b></li><li class=\"d1\">neighbor = <b>everybody</b>; don't love as yourself → sinned</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:10</b> keep whole law, stumble in one point → <b>guilty of all</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"do not commit adultery\" and \"do not murder\"</li><li class=\"d1\">murderer: \"never cheated on my wife, I'm not all bad\" - <b>\"still a murderer\"</b>, a transgressor</li><li class=\"d0\">Remember: people who think they're <b>pious, faithful</b></li><li class=\"d1\">fail to love neighbor → broken the law</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't matter if faithful to wife, at services, saying prayers, don't lie</li><li class=\"d1\">mistreat brother because he's poor - <b>or the rich man</b> who needs salvation → doesn't matter</li></ul>"},{"t":2092.68,"lv":2,"h":"2:12 - Law of liberty","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:12</b> \"speak and do as those who will be judged by the <b>law of liberty</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why \"law of freedom\", not just \"the law\"? = \"the law which sets you free\"</li><li class=\"d1\">back to <b>Paul in Romans</b>: under <i>nomos</i> / Torah, <b>letter and spirit</b> are subsections</li><li class=\"d1\">Holy Spirit <b>writes the law in our hearts</b></li><li class=\"d0\">James: law <b>fulfilled in Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">still the <b>Torah</b>, same commandments</li><li class=\"d1\">\"love your neighbor as yourself\" from <b>Leviticus</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>set free by the Spirit</b> to fulfill it, \"not in the old way\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same qualifier as Paul</li><li class=\"d1\">nuance lost: \"he just didn't like the law\" - <b>no</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: law as fulfilled in Christ vs. fellow <b>Pharisees</b> who accepted Christ and wanted to impose particular parts</li><li class=\"d0\">Speak and do - <b>works and words</b> - judged at the <b>last judgment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">we've received commandments, the word, Christ → judged by what we did with it</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ: \"judged according to our <b>works</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2244.92,"lv":3,"h":"2:13 - Judgment without mercy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:13</b> \"judgment is <b>without mercy</b> to the one who has shown no mercy\"</li><li class=\"d1\">reverse of Beatitude: <b>blessed are the merciful</b>, they will be shown mercy</li><li class=\"d0\">Show no mercy to the poor, destitute man → why expect mercy from God?</li><li class=\"d0\">Parable of the <b>evil steward</b></li><li class=\"d1\">forgiven a <b>huge debt</b>, attacked the guy who owed \"a couple of bucks\"</li><li class=\"d1\">thrown in prison - <b>forgiveness revoked</b> because he wouldn't forgive</li><li class=\"d0\">Constant Matthew theme: \"<b>forgive us our debts as we forgive our debtors</b>\" - parallel</li><li class=\"d0\">We're in the <b>judge position</b> now</li><li class=\"d1\">God entrusted this role/authority in your <b>church</b>, to help each other find salvation</li><li class=\"d1\">show partiality, no mercy, favoritism → why expect <b>mercy and no favoritism</b> when standing before God?</li></ul>"},{"t":2362.4,"lv":3,"h":"Cliffhanger: where we stop","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Now we get into the <b>controversial part</b>\" - \"Cliffhanger\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Stop at <b>end of 2:13</b>; pick up at <b>James 2:14</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Next: the section that got \"a certain old <b>Luther</b> in Germany\" upset at the Epistle of St. James</li><li class=\"d0\">Question: is it really <b>disagreeing with Paul</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">\"About to open the proverbial <b>can of worms</b>\"</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: <b>James 2:14</b> - the section that upset <b>Luther</b>; does it disagree with Paul?"});
